dimension,csv2,postgresql,advantage,basis,note
比較項目,csv2,PostgreSQL,優勢方,依據,說明
"storage, text at scale",1.00x,"roughly 1.2-1.5x, plus 20-40% per index",csv2,documented,"24-byte tuple header per row, plus alignment and page fill factor; NOT measured here"
"storage, narrow numeric rows",1.00x,up to 3-5x,csv2,documented,the fixed per-row header dominates when rows are small; NOT measured here
update one cell in 1 GiB,rewrites the whole file,"one 8 KiB page plus WAL, about 10 KiB",PostgreSQL,measured + documented,0.4 s at just 16 MiB versus 0.25 ms; the ratio grows linearly with file size
append one row,O(1) via O_APPEND,INSERT plus WAL,tie,reasoned,both are cheap; PostgreSQL adds a round trip
lookup by key,O(n) full scan,O(log n) B-tree,PostgreSQL,documented,
full scan,memchr plus parse,seq scan with MVCC visibility per row,csv2,UNMEASURED,"PostgreSQL does more work per row, but no Swift parser exists yet to compare against"
concurrency,"single writer, no locking","MVCC, many concurrent writers",PostgreSQL,documented,
transactions,none,"ACID, across statements and tables",PostgreSQL,documented,
referential integrity,none,"foreign keys, CHECK, NOT NULL, UNIQUE",PostgreSQL,documented,
NULL,cannot express it,first-class,PostgreSQL,documented,CSV cannot distinguish empty from absent; update_licenses.sh uses a sentinel instead
deployment,"one binary, no daemon",a server process to run and maintain,csv2,documented,
network access,none,"yes, with roles and permissions",PostgreSQL,documented,
git diff,"line-level, reviewable",not applicable; it is a live server,csv2,measured,decisive here: both CSV accidents in this repo were recovered from git
backup,copy the file,"pg_dump, WAL archiving, PITR",depends,documented,PostgreSQL is far more capable; csv2 is far simpler
comfortable read-write size,under 1 GiB,hundreds of GiB to a few TB,PostgreSQL,measured + documented,
hard ceiling,about 17 GiB here,32 TB per table,PostgreSQL,measured + documented,atomic rename needs 2x the size; 34 GiB free on this volume
right tool when,the file must stay reviewable text,the data outgrows one machine,,reasoned,"for anything between, SQLite is usually the answer; see vs-sqlite.csv2"
